===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|role-model}}
* {{alter|en|rôle model}}  {{qualifier|rare}}

===Etymology===
{{coin|en|occ=sociologist|Robert K. Merton}}. First use appears c. 1944 in the ''{{w|American Sociological Review}}''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[serve]]s as an [[example]], or whose [[behavior]] is [[emulate]]d by others.
#: {{syn|en|exemplar|household deity|Thesaurus:model}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=You Can Call Me Al|album=Graceland|author=w:Paul Simon|year=1986|passage=Where's my wife and family? / What if I die here? / Who'll be my '''role model''' / Now that my '''role model''' is gone, gone?}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect (video game)|Mass Effect}}|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2008|system=PC|scene=Citadel|isbn=9780784546642|oclc=246633669|passage=Shepard: I don't have time for this, Conrad. I'm not here to be a '''role model'''.<br>Conrad Verner: Oh, I see how it is. Commander Shepard doesn't have time for the little people!<br>Conrad Verner: Far be it for me to get in your way! You go be a hero.}}

